From f91fde6a27e0b2b92209e41b5e9558552fbb2363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 22:17:52 -0700
Subject: bifrost: SHMEM data plane, tracemem, vtimestamp, and aggregation
 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

W7 (per-class drop attribution): SHMEM_VERSION bumps 4 → 5. Each
per-CPU state widens from 64 B to 128 B to hold per-class arrays
(dropped_records[4], dropped_bytes[4]) indexed by
BIFROST_DROP_CLASS_{PRINCIPAL,AGG,STKSTR,DBLERR}. New
bifrost_shmem_reserve_kernel_class(size, class) entry point;
bifrost_kfunc_shmem_reserve defaults to PRINCIPAL; in-kernel
pumps (push_agg_snapshot, push_symtab_snapshot,
bifrost_kfunc_publish_vma_table) pass class explicitly.

W10 (walltimestamp / progenyof / vtimestamp): new kfuncs
bifrost_kfunc_walltime_ns (ktime_get_real_ns),
bifrost_kfunc_progenyof (RCU walk of current->real_parent,
BIFROST_PROGENYOF_MAX_DEPTH=64), and bifrost_kfunc_vtimestamp_ns
(currently aliases ktime_get_ns — proper per-thread delta
tracking deferred to iter-5, no DIF/wire change needed for the
upgrade).

W9 (string built-ins): nine new kfuncs covering strlen, copyin,
copyinstr, strchr, strrchr, strstr, index, strjoin, substr. All
share BIFROST_STR_MAX=256 bounded scratch via DEFINE_PER_CPU
(bifrost_copyinstr_scratch / _scratch_aux). KF_RET_NULL on
strchr/strrchr/strstr so the verifier requires NULL-checks.

W8 (speculation, protocol-level): bifrost_kfunc_speculation,
_speculate, _commit, _discard registered as no-op stubs so
DTrace scripts using speculation compile + load cleanly; real
per-lane side-buffer routing filed under W8 follow-on in
docs/dtrace-roadmap.md.

W5 (clear, protocol-level): bifrost_kfunc_clear_agg registered
no-op so clear(@agg) parses + lowers; KF_ARG_PTR_TO_MAP + per-CPU
map walk deferred to iter-5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
